            <div>
            <p>37 [Trial titles and early drafts of stanzas one and three of] L. of G.'S PURPORT [1891] [3] p. on 3l. (scrap and two leaves) 9&#189; x 19 to 25 x 20 cm.  H</p>
            <p>First published in <hi rend="italic">Good-Bye My Fancy</hi> (1891).</p>
           
            
            <lg type="linegroup">
                <head type="main" rend="underline"><hi rend="tripleUnderline">L</hi> of G's purport</head>
                <l>Not to exclude or take away or<lb/> pick out evils from their formed<lb/> able masses, (even to expose them,)</l>
                <l>But add, complete, extend, the immortal<lb/> good.</l>
            </lg>
            
            <note type="archival" place="bottom" hand="#h02">73</note>
